From d2e1519ba520bc25500135325755f671280a56d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:23:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): Sodick LN2W control-side wire offset (G41/G42
 H, G40 on the lead-out)

The LN2W post writes G41 / G42 Hnnn on its own line before the
straight lead-in when the stream has a COMP record (control or wear).
H is the pass number from H001; the first pass must be on C001 (the
owner: C001 always goes with H001); a later pass writes the condition
that the operation states. G40 goes on the lead-out move.

The law that other wire dialects share is a new prelude helper
(wire_offset.rs): a lead-in shorter than the offset radius, an arc
lead-in or lead-out, a side change while on, and a section that ends
with the offset on are refused by name. Output without a COMP record
does not change.

Fixes #4076

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
